course: dictionary
lesson: 2152
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one is in use. The word cord is a good example. «Tie the parcel with a cord.» Here the words tie and parcel show that cord means a thin rope or a thick string.
explain: Now read this: «Do not pull a plug out by the cord.» The plug and the wire point to a different meaning, the covered wire that joins a machine to the plug. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A rope would not make sense, so the meaning must be the wire.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Take off anything with cords before playing on a climbing frame.» If you swap in "a big pile of firewood", the sentence falls apart. So this cord is not firewood. It is a string or rope that could catch on a child.
fact: A cord is a thin rope or a thick string.
fact: A cord can also be the covered wire that joins a machine to its plug, like a phone charger cord.
fact: The spinal cord is the bundle of nerves in your backbone, and it carries messages around your body.
fact: A cord of wood is a big pile of firewood.
fact: «Your vocal cords wobble as air from your lungs passes them», and that is how your voice makes sound.
exercise: «Tie the parcel with a cord.» What is a cord here? | A nerve in your back | A plug | A pile of firewood | *A thin rope or a thick string
exercise: «Take off anything with cords before playing on a climbing frame, because they can catch and strangle a child.» Why should you remove them? | They are too short to see | They keep you warm | They make you run faster | *They can catch and strangle a child
exercise: «She stacked a cord of wood by the back door.» What does cord mean here? | A thin rope | *A big pile of firewood | A bundle of nerves | A wire to a plug
test: «When you hum, your vocal cords wobble as air from your lungs passes them.» What do the vocal cords do when you hum? | They glow | They fill with water | *They wobble | They break
test: «You should pull a plug out by holding the plug itself, not by yanking the cord.» What is the cord in this sentence? | *The covered wire that joins the machine to the plug | A bundle of nerves | A pile of wood | A thick rope for climbing
exam: Which meaning of cord fits «The spinal cord carries messages from your brain to the rest of your body»? | *A bundle of nerves in your backbone | A wire to a plug | A thin rope | A pile of firewood
